WEBVTT

00:51.332 --> 00:55.002
Okay, everyone. Hurry up and hand in
your Oscar picks before it starts.

00:56.796 --> 00:59.339
<i>Peter, for best picture
you wrote Wild Hogs.</i>

00:59.506 --> 01:04.302
Lois, four guys from the suburbs
hit the road. And the road hit back.

01:05.679 --> 01:08.682
Peter knows the advertising
log lines for every movie.

01:08.849 --> 01:11.226
<i>- Blades of Glory.
- Kick some ice.</i>

01:11.393 --> 01:13.603
<i>- Entrapment.
- The trap is set.</i>

01:13.770 --> 01:15.730
<i>- RV.
- On a family vacation...</i>

01:15.896 --> 01:17.648
...no one can hear you scream.

01:17.815 --> 01:20.401
<i>- Philadelphia.
- Poop-shoot lawsuit.</i>

01:20.568 --> 01:22.403
- I don't remember that one.
- That one doesn't sound real.

01:22.570 --> 01:24.739
<i>Ladies
and gentlemen, Scarlett Johansson...</i>

01:24.905 --> 01:27.199
<i>...and, for some reason,
Steve Buscemi.</i>

01:27.366 --> 01:28.909
Man, look at that Steve Buscemi.

01:29.076 --> 01:31.494
Every one of his teeth
is in business for itself.

01:31.661 --> 01:35.874
You know, Steve, the art director's job
is never an easy one.

01:36.040 --> 01:38.752
That's right, Scarlett. But this year...

01:38.918 --> 01:41.337
- Where are you going?
- To the Elton John party.

01:41.504 --> 01:44.257
What? I told you we were staying
for the Governors Ball.

01:44.424 --> 01:48.469
And I told you, Tim, we would see
how the evening plays out.

01:48.635 --> 01:51.430
You guys have fun.
I'm going for Scarlett.

01:51.597 --> 01:54.391
It smells like Josh Hartnett's balls
in there.

01:54.558 --> 01:56.810
Peter, may I use your restroom?

01:56.977 --> 02:01.105
I took a laxative and a stool hardener...
Oh! And they're fighting it out in there.

02:01.272 --> 02:03.191
Yeah, it's upstairs, Mort.

02:03.357 --> 02:06.152
Oh, boy.
I hope there's a scale in there.

02:06.319 --> 02:09.197
I'd like to have a before and after
on this one.

02:09.363 --> 02:11.616
- I'll be out in a minute.
- I really need to go.

02:11.782 --> 02:13.451
She said she'll be out in a minute.

02:14.285 --> 02:16.912
Oh, I hope there's another bathroom
in here. Oh, God.

02:19.289 --> 02:22.542
Oh, thank God. A Porta-Potty.

02:28.548 --> 02:30.884
Dad, Mr. Goldman never drank
his Ensure.

02:31.051 --> 02:33.135
Can I have it even though
it's dinnertime?

02:33.302 --> 02:36.263
Sure, Chris. Drink Ensure as a meal
or in-between meals.

02:36.430 --> 02:38.224
Or when you're on the go.

02:38.390 --> 02:41.560
- Is Mort still in the bathroom?
- I'll go see if he's all right.

02:42.061 --> 02:43.229
Mort?

02:43.395 --> 02:44.647
Hello? Mort?

02:44.813 --> 02:47.273
Hey, hey, hey.
What are you doing in my room?

02:47.440 --> 02:50.902
Don't touch my stuff with your
dirty walking-on-the-street paws.

02:51.069 --> 02:53.279
I'm looking for Mort.
He came up here an hour ago...

02:53.446 --> 02:55.531
...and never came back down.
- Uh-oh.

02:55.823 --> 02:58.076
- What?
- My time machine has been activated.

02:58.243 --> 03:00.703
Time machine?
I didn't know you had a time machine.

03:00.870 --> 03:04.289
Yeah, I built it after I got bored
with that European See 'n Say.

03:04.957 --> 03:07.542
<i>The pig goes, "Whack. "</i>

03:09.002 --> 03:12.130
<i>The cow goes, "Shazoo. "</i>

03:12.297 --> 03:14.800
It most certainly does not.

03:14.967 --> 03:17.927
<i>The rooster goes, "Gee-gree-gee. "</i>

03:18.094 --> 03:20.263
Where?
Where does the rooster say that?

03:20.429 --> 03:22.515
<i>The monkey goes, "Magack. "</i>

03:22.682 --> 03:25.309
Oh, no, no, no, it does not.

03:25.476 --> 03:27.645
<i>The elephant goes, "Voo-arp. "</i>

03:27.812 --> 03:29.105
Yeah, kind of.

03:29.271 --> 03:32.775
Stewie, do you think Mort accidentally
stumbled into the time machine?

03:32.942 --> 03:34.192
I suppose it's possible.

03:34.359 --> 03:38.780
<i>Let's ask Rick Moranis and the back-up
singers from Little Shop of Horrors.</i>

03:38.947 --> 03:41.741
<i>I saw a red-headed guy
Come up here about an hour ago</i>

03:41.908 --> 03:43.368
<i>Mort the Jew</i>

03:43.535 --> 03:46.496
<i>He seemed to be in a rush
And had a pained look on his face</i>

03:46.663 --> 03:48.415
<i>Had to poo</i>

03:48.580 --> 03:50.290
<i>Sha-doo ba doo ba doo</i>

03:50.457 --> 03:52.167
<i>And he stepped into that box there</i>

03:52.334 --> 03:54.503
<i>And suddenly
There was a big flash of light</i>

03:54.670 --> 03:58.507
<i>That's when he went back in time</i>

03:58.674 --> 04:01.635
We have to get him back.
Where did the machine send him?

04:01.802 --> 04:04.679
- I don't know.
- How can you not? It's a time machine.

04:04.846 --> 04:07.348
Doesn't it have a display
that tells the year?

04:07.515 --> 04:10.435
Is my time machine not as good
as your time machine?

04:10.601 --> 04:13.813
Oh, yeah. Oh, no, you probably got
a way better time machine. Yeah.

04:13.980 --> 04:15.106
Stupid dog.

04:15.273 --> 04:18.192
Then can't you press a couple of buttons
and bring him back?

04:18.359 --> 04:20.861
No, he can't just come back.
He needs the return pad.

04:21.027 --> 04:23.113
Well, we can't just leave Mort
back in time.

04:23.280 --> 04:25.949
That would be more irresponsible
than silent-movie porn.

04:42.006 --> 04:43.424
All right, we'll go get him.

04:43.591 --> 04:46.761
But remember, Brian, don't touch
anything when we're in the past.

04:46.927 --> 04:49.805
Even stepping on a mosquito
could create a chain reaction...

04:49.972 --> 04:51.389
...that alters the present.

04:51.556 --> 04:53.725
- Really?
- No, you can do whatever you want.

04:53.892 --> 04:55.393
Come on.

05:04.611 --> 05:06.445
Okay, if everything worked properly...

05:06.612 --> 05:09.490
...this should be the exact time
and place Mort was sent to.

05:09.656 --> 05:12.618
- We just gotta figure out where we are.
- Or when we are.

05:12.784 --> 05:15.329
Oh, that's such
a douche time-traveler thing to say.

05:15.496 --> 05:17.247
Shazoo.

05:17.414 --> 05:19.875
Okay, we're somewhere in Europe. Aha!

05:20.042 --> 05:21.125
Look, Brian.

05:21.292 --> 05:23.836
This trail of used tissues
should lead right to Mort.

05:24.003 --> 05:25.171
Or to Quagmire.

05:26.589 --> 05:28.257
Oh, he's gross.

05:51.363 --> 05:54.073
Warsaw?
Well, at least we know where we are.

05:54.532 --> 05:56.450
RABBl:
And so we had him crucified.

05:56.617 --> 05:59.536
But that doesn't leave this room.
Anyway, the point is...

05:59.703 --> 06:04.041
...may Chaim and Sarah have many
wonderful years together. Amen.

06:04.208 --> 06:08.586
Excuse me,
we're looking for a Mr. Goldman.

06:08.962 --> 06:10.213
Mr. Mort Goldman.

06:11.798 --> 06:15.134
A small-business owner, tends to whine
a lot, kind of a hypochondriac.

06:16.427 --> 06:20.056
Oh, no. You can't put your hand back up
after you put it down. Never mind.

06:20.556 --> 06:24.768
Stewie, look at this.
"September 1, 1939."

06:24.977 --> 06:27.062
There's something about that date.

06:27.229 --> 06:30.315
<i>I now pronounce you man and wife.
Mazletof.</i>

06:30.482 --> 06:31.817
Now step on the glass.

06:31.984 --> 06:33.860
Oh, but be careful, though.

06:34.027 --> 06:36.154
At my wedding,
I cut myself on the glass.

06:36.321 --> 06:38.489
When I got to Palm Beach
for the honeymoon...

06:38.656 --> 06:42.118
...I had to put a Wonder Bread bag
on my foot to keep the sand out.

06:42.576 --> 06:44.078
<i>Mazletof!</i>

06:46.580 --> 06:47.915
Oh, Mort. Thank God.

06:48.082 --> 06:50.501
Brian and Stewie?
You're in heaven too?

06:50.668 --> 06:53.545
Mort, this isn't heaven.
You've time-traveled into the past.

06:53.712 --> 06:56.339
What? How is that possible?

06:56.506 --> 06:58.633
Just trust me.
We're here to bring you home.

06:58.800 --> 07:00.719
But it's gotta be heaven, Brian. Look.

07:00.885 --> 07:03.972
There's my frugal Aunt Ruth,
my thrifty Uncle Isaac...

07:04.139 --> 07:05.849
...my bargain-hunting Aunt Flo...

07:06.016 --> 07:09.351
...and my Great-Aunt Vera who didn't
like to spend a lot on anything.

07:09.518 --> 07:10.853
We gotta get out of here.

07:11.020 --> 07:13.397
But, Brian, when am I gonna
have another chance...

07:13.564 --> 07:16.567
...to see my Grandpa Chaim's wedding
with my own eyes?

07:16.734 --> 07:17.985
Yes, he's right, Brian.

07:18.152 --> 07:20.320
Besides, I've never been
to a Hebrew wedding.

07:20.487 --> 07:23.032
Well, I guess we could stay
a little longer.

07:23.198 --> 07:25.825
Oh, wonderful.
I wanna be hoisted up on the chair...

07:25.992 --> 07:28.327
...and see what it feels like
to be top Jew.

08:53.533 --> 08:54.617
Uh-oh.

09:10.674 --> 09:12.967
I knew there was something
about this date.

09:13.133 --> 09:16.470
September 1 st, 1939.
This is the German invasion of Poland.

09:16.637 --> 09:20.015
It's also the exact day and year
that Rene Russo was born.

09:20.182 --> 09:22.810
We gotta get out of here fast.
Set up the return pad...

09:22.977 --> 09:25.771
...and let's get back to our own time.
- Right.

09:29.399 --> 09:31.567
- What? Why are we still here?
- I don't know.

09:31.734 --> 09:32.944
- It's not working.
- Yeah.

09:33.111 --> 09:35.405
You know what's not gonna fix it?
Your shouting.

09:35.571 --> 09:37.532
Oh, God.
Should we ask somebody for help?

09:37.699 --> 09:41.077
Yeah, right. How many Polacks
does it take to fix a time machine?

09:41.244 --> 09:42.453
Well, we can't stay here.

09:42.620 --> 09:46.164
We'll have to get Mort to England.
It's the only place he'll be safe.

09:46.331 --> 09:48.083
Oh, they're awful, those Nazis.

09:48.250 --> 09:50.711
If they catch me,
they'll beat me unmerciful...

09:50.877 --> 09:54.548
...and rub dirt in my ass, neck,
and all over my antsy nipples.

09:54.715 --> 09:56.216
What?

10:06.726 --> 10:07.893
There's the checkpoint.

10:08.060 --> 10:10.438
If we get passed it,
we're out of occupied Poland.

10:10.604 --> 10:14.149
- Right. Mort, you all set?
- Oh, God. I hope this works.

10:15.817 --> 10:17.902
Hello. We'd like to leave Poland now.

10:18.069 --> 10:21.573
We'll be bringing our friend, who is
absolutely 100 percent not Jewish.

10:21.740 --> 10:24.576
Hey, how about that Jesus, huh?
What a guy.

10:24.743 --> 10:26.661
Father, we are so glad you're here.

10:26.828 --> 10:29.872
We need you to conduct last rites
for our friend over there.

10:32.124 --> 10:34.668
Well, I suppose.

10:34.835 --> 10:39.089
Dear God, the non-Jewish god,
be a mensch...

10:39.256 --> 10:40.549
Ahem.

10:40.716 --> 10:43.677
I mean, a good guy,
because it says in the old book...

10:43.844 --> 10:45.386
Not so old, though.

10:45.553 --> 10:47.680
You know, still good. Still good.

10:47.847 --> 10:50.141
Still some things... Good things to say.

10:51.934 --> 10:55.313
We pray in the name of you
and of your son...

10:55.480 --> 10:59.650
...who died in a freak accident
that you can't really blame on anyone...

10:59.816 --> 11:01.109
Ahem.

11:01.276 --> 11:04.196
Take this man up
to your retail paying place.

11:04.404 --> 11:06.823
Are you sure you're a real priest?

11:06.990 --> 11:10.786
Yeah. Yeah, I can vouch for him.
He's real. He's molested me many times.

11:10.952 --> 11:16.081
Sorry I'm late. I was busy doing
innocent non-molesty things.

11:16.248 --> 11:18.083
Wait a minute, two priests?

11:18.250 --> 11:20.002
That is impossible.

11:20.169 --> 11:21.712
This collar comes right off.

11:21.879 --> 11:23.255
He's a filthy Jew!

11:23.422 --> 11:25.508
Oh, boy. You should be glad...

11:25.674 --> 11:28.803
...your Human Resources person
was not around to hear that.

11:28.969 --> 11:30.595
Run.

11:52.407 --> 11:54.743
Hey, buddy, I need to borrow this.

12:24.980 --> 12:26.606
<i>Das poop!</i>

12:28.775 --> 12:31.278
I wanna get back on
the motorcycle.

12:31.444 --> 12:34.405
- I told you, it's out of gas.
- Why isn't the time machine working?

12:34.572 --> 12:36.740
- I don't know, Mort.
- I hate it here.

12:36.907 --> 12:40.536
I hate this whole goddamn place.
It's all a bunch of shit.

12:40.703 --> 12:42.746
It's all a bunch
of goddamn shit.

12:42.913 --> 12:45.749
- Okay, take it easy, man.
- No. Fuck you, Stewie.

12:45.916 --> 12:50.295
I'm a Jew in Nazi-occupied Europe.
Fuck you. Fuck the both of you.

12:50.461 --> 12:52.130
- I didn't say anything.
- Oh, thanks, Brian.

12:52.297 --> 12:54.507
- This is a bunch of shit!
- Okay, you know what, Mort?

12:54.674 --> 12:56.342
Shut up! All right?
Just shut the fuck up.

12:56.509 --> 12:59.053
I don't give a shit about you.
You know, we could just leave you here.

12:59.220 --> 13:01.139
Yeah, right. Just leave me here.
That's great.

13:01.306 --> 13:04.599
We're in occupied Europe.
And if you haven't noticed, I'm Jewish.

13:04.766 --> 13:06.977
Oh, I noticed.
Helen Keller would notice.

13:08.353 --> 13:10.772
- Eat my ass, Brian.
- Don't you mean your ass neck?

13:10.939 --> 13:12.691
Shut up. That's a real thing.

13:53.520 --> 13:55.481
Well, Nazis. That's refreshing.

13:57.941 --> 14:00.569
All right, on three,
we'll make for the closest U-boat.

14:20.378 --> 14:21.713
Everybody, hang on.

14:33.016 --> 14:34.768
We're being pursued by two objects.

14:34.935 --> 14:37.478
Looks like one's another U-boat.

14:38.312 --> 14:41.482
The other appears to be
Terence Trent D'Arby.

14:48.906 --> 14:50.366
Fire.

14:53.910 --> 14:54.953
- Uh-oh.
- What?

14:55.119 --> 14:57.789
- Hold on to something.
- Why isn't the time machine working?

14:57.956 --> 14:59.040
I swear to God, Mort...

14:59.207 --> 15:02.043
...I will stuff you in a torpedo tube
and crush you against the sea.

15:12.594 --> 15:15.847
Brian, I've got an idea.
It's a long shot, but it just might work.

15:16.014 --> 15:17.307
- See that newspaper?
- Yeah.

15:17.474 --> 15:19.643
Stuff it in the waste tube.

15:42.872 --> 15:44.583
Can you hand me the radio?

15:44.749 --> 15:47.419
Thanks. Hi, this is car...

15:47.586 --> 15:49.963
- What number are we?
- Five-five.

15:50.130 --> 15:53.132
Car 55. We're in a sub.

15:59.763 --> 16:01.557
Oh, my God. It's England.

16:01.724 --> 16:03.517
We've reached England. We're saved.

16:03.684 --> 16:05.436
Really? Are you sure it's England?

16:05.602 --> 16:07.937
Yes, I can see
the white cliffs of Dover.

16:08.104 --> 16:10.481
Boy, they weren't kidding.
Those things are white.

16:10.690 --> 16:13.443
So we're gonna take the whole family
on vacation this summer.

16:13.609 --> 16:15.903
Load up the Country Squire
and head up to New Hampshire.

16:16.070 --> 16:19.032
By the way, thanks for
the recommendation. Great cheese shop.

16:19.198 --> 16:22.410
Yeah. You know, our youngest has been
accepted to Northfield Mount Hermon.

16:22.577 --> 16:24.953
Oh, gosh.
Is Warren in high school already?

16:25.120 --> 16:28.290
Yeah. You know, a funny thing happened
to me on the way to middle age.

16:28.457 --> 16:29.791
My kids grew up.

16:31.752 --> 16:33.628
Say, you know, when you take
that vacation...

16:33.795 --> 16:35.547
...don't forget traveler's insurance.

16:35.714 --> 16:38.091
A lot of people do,
and a lot of people are sorry.

16:41.594 --> 16:42.970
London in wartime.

16:43.137 --> 16:44.930
This is history right here, Brian.

16:45.097 --> 16:47.099
And look, there's Winston Churchill.

16:47.266 --> 16:50.102
Maybe we'll get an up-close look
at his legendary wit.

16:50.269 --> 16:53.689
Oh, Winston. Drunk again, I see.

16:53.856 --> 16:55.482
Yeah, well, you're a cunt.

16:55.648 --> 16:56.858
Wickedly funny.

16:58.651 --> 17:01.446
I guess history has just
whittled it down to the gems.

17:04.741 --> 17:08.620
- Why isn't the time machine working?
- I'm working on it, Mort, all right?

17:08.787 --> 17:11.705
- Oh, here's the problem.
What is it?

17:11.872 --> 17:15.167
The transfer circuits are powered
by uranium and this is tapped out.

17:15.334 --> 17:17.419
Are you saying we need
to find some uranium?

17:17.586 --> 17:18.670
I'm afraid so.

17:18.837 --> 17:21.465
But where do we find uranium
in World War II Europe?

17:21.632 --> 17:23.050
There's only one place.

17:23.217 --> 17:25.927
At the top-secret
atomic-research facility...

17:26.094 --> 17:27.178
...in Berlin.

17:27.345 --> 17:30.181
Wait, Germany's building weapons
of mass destruction?

17:30.348 --> 17:32.767
Why doesn't America go there
and kick their asses?

17:32.934 --> 17:35.895
I don't know.
Maybe because they don't have any oil.

17:36.062 --> 17:40.273
Oh. Clap, clap, clap.

17:44.820 --> 17:48.406
- I don't know. I don't wanna do this.
- Berlin is the closest place...

17:48.573 --> 17:51.409
...we're gonna find uranium.
It's the only way to get home.

17:51.576 --> 17:55.205
Men, as officers of the Royal Air Force,
you're the very best in the world.

17:55.372 --> 17:58.165
However, this mission to Germany
will not be an easy one.

17:58.332 --> 18:00.918
Four-and-a-half of every five of you
will not return.

18:01.085 --> 18:03.879
Half of Jenson there can tell you,
it gets pretty sticky.

18:04.046 --> 18:06.715
But I never lost my good spirits,
I haven't.

18:06.882 --> 18:08.759
So let's get up there, be safe...

18:08.926 --> 18:12.637
...and get back to the big, fat pigs
of wives we have waiting at home.

18:12.804 --> 18:15.723
- Pardon me, I'd like to join.
- What are your qualifications?

18:15.890 --> 18:18.601
I have a British accent,
I'm possibly homosexual...

18:18.768 --> 18:20.353
...and my wife is ghastly.

18:20.520 --> 18:22.188
Bombs away.

18:29.361 --> 18:31.405
- Talk to me, Goose.
- Don't call me that.

18:31.572 --> 18:35.242
You're my eyes, Goose.
Keep an eye out for those Krauts.

18:35.409 --> 18:36.702
Uh-oh. Germans dead ahead.

19:33.171 --> 19:35.673
It's another wave of fighters.
We're outnumbered.

19:35.840 --> 19:37.925
Oh, no, we're not.

19:38.092 --> 19:40.428
Stand by, my Hawkmen.

19:40.595 --> 19:42.597
Dive!

20:11.957 --> 20:15.543
Oh, my God and baby Jesus!
We're going down!

20:16.294 --> 20:18.171
Quick, get the parachutes.

20:18.338 --> 20:20.715
There are no parachutes.
All I can find was this.

20:20.882 --> 20:26.638
A raft? We're not sinking.
We're crashing!

20:55.373 --> 20:57.750
- Where are we?
- I think we're in Germany.

20:57.917 --> 20:59.460
Look, there's the Black Forest.

20:59.627 --> 21:02.170
We gonna take the whole family
on vacation this summer.

21:02.337 --> 21:05.507
The 10 of us gonna load up the Impala
and head on down to Hotlanta.

21:05.674 --> 21:08.635
Hey, I heard that. Hey, thanks for
the tip on that check-cashing place.

21:08.802 --> 21:10.428
I was in and out with
one ID.

21:10.595 --> 21:12.430
You know my boy
is out on bail next week, right?

21:12.597 --> 21:14.891
Man. It seems like yesterday
he was in juvie.

21:15.058 --> 21:17.434
Hey. Say, man, when you
on your trip...

21:17.601 --> 21:20.646
...skip that traveler's insurance.
That's a rip-off.

21:23.983 --> 21:26.902
There it is. Berlin.

21:27.444 --> 21:28.988
So this is Berlin, huh?

21:29.154 --> 21:30.698
Doesn't seem so bad.

21:30.865 --> 21:32.657
Dear God, this place is nightmarish.

21:32.824 --> 21:35.743
Look at the offensive way
they draw Jewish people.

21:43.042 --> 21:46.129
It's here. The uranium lab is in here.

21:46.503 --> 21:48.046
- Where'd you get that thing?
- Up your ass.

21:48.213 --> 21:49.256
- What?
- What?

21:51.091 --> 21:54.094
Hey, fellas,
you want to get a free caricature?

21:54.261 --> 21:56.930
- Yeah.
- I want to be a skateboarder.

22:03.019 --> 22:04.478
There's something on here.

22:05.146 --> 22:07.356
Huh, that's weird.

22:07.523 --> 22:09.775
All right, come on.
Let's get inside that lab.

22:19.784 --> 22:22.454
- Hey, guys.
Hitler!

22:22.621 --> 22:23.955
How's it going, Mr. Hitler?

22:24.122 --> 22:26.833
Oh, it's a dog-eat-dog Reich
and I'm wearing bacon pants.

22:28.543 --> 22:31.755
- So how's the atomic bomb coming?
- It's coming. It's coming.

22:31.921 --> 22:34.173
There are problems.
We're having better luck...

22:34.340 --> 22:38.218
<i>...developing this impressive collection
of 100 luftballons.</i>

22:38.385 --> 22:39.511
Oh, damn.

22:39.678 --> 22:41.847
I guess we'll just let you
get back to work.

22:42.014 --> 22:43.307
Oh, I almost forgot.

22:43.474 --> 22:46.101
I don't suppose you boys
have uranium I could borrow?

22:46.268 --> 22:47.394
Oh, of course.

22:47.561 --> 22:49.645
Give him some uranium,
Mean Joe Green.

22:49.812 --> 22:51.814
Hey, kid. Catch.

22:52.231 --> 22:53.649
Thanks, Mean Joe.

22:53.816 --> 22:56.319
- He's not really mean at all.
- No, he's a nice guy.

23:00.073 --> 23:01.866
Okay, the time machine is refueled.

23:02.033 --> 23:05.660
Let's find a safe spot
and make the trip back home.

23:39.567 --> 23:41.486
Arrest him! Arrest those three!

23:41.653 --> 23:44.280
These filth are making a mockery
of our Reich.

23:44.447 --> 23:46.616
Execute them!

23:47.408 --> 23:49.577
- Unless...
- Unless what?

23:49.743 --> 23:53.372
Unless they can sing
a charming musical number.

23:55.499 --> 23:56.667
<i>Whenever...</i>

23:56.834 --> 24:00.879
Damn it, will you two just get
in the fucking time machine?

24:05.258 --> 24:07.593
We did it. We're home.
Everything's fine.

24:07.760 --> 24:10.388
- Uh... Well, not quite.
- What do you mean?

24:10.555 --> 24:13.099
Aren't you nervous Mort knows
all about this stuff?

24:13.266 --> 24:15.184
Oh, I'm one step ahead of you, Brian.

24:15.351 --> 24:18.938
See, we've arrived 30 seconds before
Mort came up to use the bathroom.

24:19.105 --> 24:22.440
Only this time, things are gonna play out
a bit differently.

24:25.652 --> 24:26.736
Can I poop in here?

24:26.903 --> 24:27.988
- No.
- No.

24:28.196 --> 24:29.281
Too late.

24:29.282 --> 25:30.282
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru